course: dictionary
lesson: 2118
title: Where paths meet
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Convergence comes from the idea of things moving towards each other and meeting. The sentence gives the clue: «A giraffe has 7 neck bones and a sauropod had 12 to 19; unrelated animals finding the same answer to reaching high food is called convergence.» The animals are not related, yet they reached the same answer, so convergence means coming together at one point.
explain: Convergence has more than one meaning, so check the subject first. In maths, it means a list of numbers getting closer and closer to one fixed number. In geography, it means two plates of the Earth's crust pushing towards each other. In everyday talk, it can mean ideas or people becoming more alike.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «Unrelated animals finding the same answer» fits well with «coming together», so your guess works. The opposite of convergence is divergence, which means moving apart.
fact: Convergence is a noun: it names a meeting point or a coming together.
fact: A «point of convergence» is the place where lines, roads or paths meet.
fact: In maths, 1/2, 3/4 and 7/8 show convergence towards 1, because they get closer and closer to it.
fact: In geography, the convergence of two plates can build mountains and volcanoes.
fact: The opposite of convergence is divergence, when things move apart.
exercise: «A giraffe has 7 neck bones and a sauropod had 12 to 19.» What does convergence describe in this sentence? | Bones turning into two separate bones | A long neck that breaks easily | Two animals from the same family | *Unrelated animals finding the same answer to reaching high food
exercise: In maths, 1/2, 3/4 and 7/8 get closer and closer to 1. What is this called? | Division | *Convergence | Conversation | Divergence
exercise: Which word means things moving apart, the opposite of convergence? | Convergence | *Divergence | Emergence | Confidence
test: In geography, what can the convergence of two plates create? | Deserts with no rain | *Mountains and volcanoes | Calm seas with no waves | Flat, empty plains
test: Which phrase means that people's ideas are becoming more alike? | Loss of memory | Sudden silence | Divergence of ideas | *Convergence of ideas
exam: Which meaning fits convergence in the sentence about the giraffe and the sauropod? | A sudden split into two separate groups | A long word for a long walk | *Unrelated things reaching the same answer by different paths | Related animals sharing one parent
